       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in unstable brady:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " temporizing, w transcutaneous pacing and/or isoproterenol"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Dose:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " IV, titrated to HR · PR interval · BP & Sx; w CAD limit total dose to 0.03–0.04 mg/kg (2–3 mg) to ⍉tachy raising myocard O2 demand"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "SE (antimuscarinic):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " dry mouth · blurred vision · photophobia & tachy are common; anhidrosis can cause heat intol; constipation & difficulty urinating may occur in elderly"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "OD:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " short-acting barbiturate or diazepam for marked excitement & convulsions; physostigmine 1–4 mg by slow IV inj rapidly reverses delirium & coma, but rapidly destroyed, so repeat doses may be needed"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
